(Stage 1c — predicates survive list reallocation. The initial list
 capacity is 8; appending beyond it forces _list_append to realloc. Stage
 1a preserves the per-slot tag (in dl) across realloc, so predicates
 classify every element correctly even after the move. Acceptance 5.)

a list called "m" is [].
append 1 to m.
append "x" to m.
append 2 to m.
append "y" to m.
append 3 to m.
append "z" to m.
append 4 to m.
append "w" to m.
append 5 to m.
append "v" to m.
For each item in m,
  if item is a text, print "T",
  otherwise print "N".